From b6f23d98f5621b01527bbad4f873c2e1273152c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: juansolo457 <5344231+Juansolo457@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 06:18:32 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Create the achievement notification dialog lazily on Windows
 too

fear-nx already does this on Switch: a dialog registers itself as a UI
drawer for its whole life, and with any UI drawer registered the presenter
paints from the UI thread. On Windows the idle dialog kept the UI thread
presenting, its present held the Vulkan queue lock for most of each frame,
and the guest output thread waited on that lock (13-15 ms per frame in
F.E.A.R.).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/ui/rex_app.cpp | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/ui/rex_app.cpp b/src/ui/rex_app.cpp
index e881af6..b7f4670 100644
--- a/src/ui/rex_app.cpp
+++ b/src/ui/rex_app.cpp
@@ -517,7 +517,10 @@ void ReXApp::LaunchModule() {
     // Register the achievement notification callback now that the runtime and
     // KernelState are guaranteed to exist. Done here (not OnCreateDialogs)
     // because KernelState is null during SetupPresentation.
-#if REX_PLATFORM_SWITCH
+    // On every platform, not only Switch: on Windows the idle dialog kept painting on the UI
+    // thread, whose present held the Vulkan queue lock most of each frame, and the guest
+    // output thread waited on that lock (F.E.A.R. held near 60 fps at a 240 Hz vblank).
+#if 1
     // Created on the first achievement, not here. A dialog registers itself as a
     // UI drawer for its whole life, and with any UI drawer registered the presenter
     // paints from the UI thread and coalesces requests, discarding frames whose GPU
